in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rash"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "quick, without thinking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At least you should go talk to Ms. Moore about before you make a rash decision."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le03ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about an important decision about work."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "job satisfaction"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "measurement of how much you enjoy your work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Having done an online test for people about job satisfaction, I realized a lot of things."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le03ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "career growth"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "advancing in a career field by getting positions with increasing responsibility"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: From what I see, my potential for career growth is limited."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le03ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "red flag"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a clue there may be some problems you haven't seen yet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There were a lot of red flags working here."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le03ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dead-end job"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a position that does not lead to advancement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How will I know if I am good enough to be a real journalist, if I am stuck in a dead-end job?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le03ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "recognition"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling you are valued and given credit for your good work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't feel that I'm being given much recognition."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le03ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "you have to play the game"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " it is necessary to obey rules, meet expectations and follow conventions in a social context (such as the workplace)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Having been here only a few months, it's too early for us to make a decision like that. We have to play the game."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le03ob10aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le03ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Perfect Infinitive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " The Perfect tenses can be used to talk about how something in the past relates to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Look at the chart for an outline of the structure and the uses of the Perfect infinitive."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" after link verbs (<span class=\\\"italic\\\">seem </span>and <span class=\\\"italic\\\">appear</span>) to refer to a previous time period\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There <span class=\\\"strong\\\">seems to have been </span>some kind of error.</span> <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">The matter <span class=\\\"strong\\\">appears to have been </span>resolved.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"verb + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">to have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"after phrases expressing emotions and feelings\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm <span class=\\\"strong\\\">sorry to have kept </span>the results from you.</span> <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">She was <span class=\\\"strong\\\">felt to have met </span>the hiring requirements.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" verb + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">to have</span> + past participle\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'm sorry to have kept you in suspense, but I want you know that things aren't going so well for me here at BFP."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There seems to have been some movement recently in the company. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She was felt not to have met the standards required."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Perfect <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about results and time, you can use a Perfect <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> form to emphasize the one thing that happens before another."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I didn't remember having done</span> the report."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here, \u201cdoing the report\u201d comes first, \u201cremembering\u201d comes next."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Having finished the prep work, she started writing.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Having met so many great colleagues here, I know we are treated with respect. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Having been here only a few months, it's too early for us to make a decision like that. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't remember having met her before."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the \u2013ing form like a noun, like an adjective or like a verb. <br/>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Smoking is dangerous. (noun)  I have a long working day. (adjective)  I don't like skiing. (verb)</span> <br/> <br/>  When you use -ing as a noun, you may or may not put an article before it.  <br/> For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Marketing is a very inexact science. The marketing of the product will continue for a few months yet.  </span> <br/> <br/>You can also use it as a noun phrase.   <br/>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Speaking to an audience is always terrifying. Swimming after work is very refreshing. </span>  <br/> <br/> You can use the -ing form before a noun when it is an adjective. <br/>  For example:</br> <span class=\"italic\"> I was met by a welcoming party at the airport. Let's go to the meeting room. </span> <br/> <br/> You use the \u2013ing form after prepositions.   <br/>For example:  </br><span class=\"italic\">Before coming, you need to speak to Tanya. After discussing it with her, I've changed my mind. I'm looking forward to seeing her again.</span>  <br/> "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, discuss the factors of job satisfaction that were mentioned in this lesson."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of other factors influencing job satisfaction. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue of 8 - 12 lines. One person wants to quit their job.  They explain why. The other person gives reasons for them to stay."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles and practice the dialogue again."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss things that influence job satisfaction."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give reasons for being unhappy at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give reasons to stay at a job."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express emotions and feelings."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about results in time. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain my ideas and opinions with precision."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Have you ever considered quitting a job? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Did someone else convince you to stay? What did they say?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "That's it ... I quit!"}], "id": 0}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "respon